WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.361
UV light can cause adjacent cytosines and thymines to form covalent bonds. The

00:00:05.361 --> 00:00:10.722
resulting distortion in the DNA backbone interferes with normal copying and transcription. This

00:00:10.722 --> 00:00:16.083
is damage that must be recognized and removed.

00:00:16.083 --> 00:00:20.583
Repair proteins recognize the damaged site. Enzymes cut the backbone on either side

00:00:20.583 --> 00:00:25.083
of the problem and remove the damaged section from that strand. The diagram

00:00:25.083 --> 00:00:29.583
shows the gap left by that removal.

00:00:29.583 --> 00:00:35.056
The missing section is replaced with correct DNA nucleotides. The backbone is then

00:00:35.056 --> 00:00:40.528
resealed by forming phosphodiester linkages. Remember the sequence: recognize the damage, cut out

00:00:40.528 --> 00:00:46.000
the section, replace it, and reseal the backbone.
